  "id": "COMPOUND:585 - PROTEIN:433",
  "verbalization": "Thiopental is implicated in the relationship with Glutathione synthetase through a multi-step mechanism involving the gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) receptor subunit alpha-6. This receptor is targeted by Thiopental, which in turn influences the activity of heptabarbital and another compound, Dihydro-2-thioxo-5-((5-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-2-furanyl)methyl)-4,6(1H,5H)-pyrimidinedione. These compounds ultimately act as targets for Glutathione synthetase. The evidence suggests that Thiopental may modulate the GABA receptor subunit alpha-6, which in turn affects the activity of these other compounds, leading to a downstream effect on Glutathione synthetase. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Thiopental could influence glutathione synthesis, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Thiopental and Glutathione synthetase, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of each component in this relationship.",
